          "level": "fallback",
          "precedentId": "seed-t4c",
          "summary": "Make PB's at-will exit unconditional on 90 days' notice, cap the exit fee at 3 months' Development Costs, and limit SFJ's discretionary exits to the end of the then-current Term on 90 days' notice.",
          "comment": "[Playbook] We removed the $60 million funding gate and pre-approval cut-off so PB may terminate for convenience on 90 days' notice, capped the exit payment at three (3) months' Development Costs instead of the 300% multiple, and limited SFJ's discretionary terminations under §§ 14.2.6 and 14.2.10 to the end of the then-current Term on 90 days' notice. This is our fallback position on customer convenience exits.",
          "ops": [
            {
              "kind": "replace",
              "paragraphId": "p0755",
              "oldText": "PB may terminate this Agreement at any time after SFJ has paid or incurred a total of $60 million of Development Costs and prior to the date of receipt of the first Regulatory Approval upon [***] prior written notice to SFJ. In the event that PB terminates this Agreement pursuant to this Section 14.2.2 then in exchange for purchasing the Trial Data Package including the Research Results included therein as set forth in Section 11.1.1.4, PB will pay SFJ, within [***] of the date of termination, an amount equal to three hundred percent (300%) of Development Costs paid or incurred by SFJ prior to such termination.",
              "newText": "PB may terminate this Agreement at any time for convenience upon 90 days' prior written notice to SFJ. In the event that PB terminates this Agreement pursuant to this Section 14.2.2 then in exchange for purchasing the Trial Data Package including the Research Results included therein as set forth in Section 11.1.1.4, PB will pay SFJ, within [***] of the date of termination, an amount not exceeding three (3) months' Development Costs as the sole early-termination fee."
            },
            {
              "kind": "insert_after",
              "paragraphId": "p0781",
              "numbering": "14.2.11",
              "text": "Any termination by SFJ in its sole discretion pursuant to Section 14.2.6 or Section 14.2.10 may be effective only at the end of the then-current Term and only upon 90 days' prior written notice to PB."
            }
          ]
